abstract: >
  An end-to-end machine learning regression project that predicts residential property sale prices using the Ames Housing Dataset. 
  The project explores relationships between property features and sale prices, neighborhood and zoning characteristics, 
  property types, historical market trends, and price segmentation. It includes data cleaning, preprocessing, feature engineering, 
  baseline model development, hyperparameter tuning, and final model evaluation. The project also translates analytical findings 
  into interpretable insights about key property price drivers and actionable recommendations for real estate valuation. 
  It demonstrates a reproducible data science workflow covering exploratory data analysis, feature engineering, regression modeling, 
  and business-oriented interpretation.

